      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "Since two of the roots of the cubic polynomial are 3 and -2, we can write the polynomial in its factored form as\n\\[a(x-3)(x+2)(x-r),\\]\nwhere r is the third root of the polynomial. Expanding this, we get\n\\[a(x^3 + (r-1)x^2 + (2-r)x - 6r).\\]\nComparing coefficients with the original equation $\\;ax^3+bx^2+cx+d=0$, we see that\n\\begin{align*}\nb &= a(r-1), \\\\\nc &= a(2-r), \\\\\nd &= -6ar.\n\\end{align*}\nTherefore,\n\\[\\frac{b+c}{a} = \\frac{a(r-1) + a(2-r)}{a} = r - 1 + 2 - r = 1.\\]",
