      "text": "Let $r_1, r_2,$ and $r_3$ be the three roots of the cubic. By Vieta's formulas, we know that\n\\begin{align*}\nr_1+ r_2+ r_3 &= \\frac{-(b/a)}{1/a}, & r_1r_2+r_2r_3+r_3r_1 &= \\frac{c/a}{1/a}, & r_3r_1r_2 &= -\\frac{d}{1/a}.\n\\end{align*}\nSince $r_1=3$ and $r_2=-2,$ this gives us that $r_3=2,$ $r_1r_2+r_2r_3+r_3r_1=5,$ and $r_1r_2r_3=-6.$ Plugging these back in, we find that \\[\\frac{r_1+r_2+r_3}{a}=\\frac{(r_3)(r_1r_2+r_1r_3+r_2r_3)}{a}=\\frac{r_3}{a}\\frac{r_1r_2r_3}{a}=\\frac{2}{a}\\frac{-6}{a}=-\\frac{12}{a}.\\]Hence, $\\frac{b+c}{a}=\\frac{1}{a}\\frac{(r_1+r_2+r_3)}{a}-0=\\boxed{-\\frac{12}{a}}.$. The answer is -\\frac{12}{a}",
